# AutoScribe Product Refinement Roadmap

This roadmap assumes:

* You are solo-building
* You already have MVP functionality
* Goal = make it feel like a real AI SaaS product
* Focus = UX + product quality, not feature quantity

---

# Sprint 1 — UX Foundation Cleanup

## Duration: 5–7 days

## Goal

Reduce chaos and make the UI feel structured.

---

## Tasks

### Frontend Architecture

* Remove massive inline styles
* Move to Tailwind consistently
* Create reusable UI primitives:

  * Button
  * Card
  * Modal
  * Input
  * StatusBadge
  * SectionHeader

---

### Layout Cleanup

* Reduce border overuse
* Improve spacing hierarchy
* Add consistent padding system
* Improve typography scale

---

### Dashboard Simplification

Reduce visible complexity:

* move advanced tools lower
* emphasize primary workflow
* reduce visual noise

---

### Responsive Fixes

Test:

* mobile
* tablet
* laptop

Fix:

* sidebar collapse
* button wrapping
* overflow
* modal sizing

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 1:

* UI feels cleaner
* app feels calmer
* codebase becomes maintainable

---

# Sprint 2 — Workflow & Onboarding

## Duration: 5–7 days

## Goal

Make users instantly understand the product.

---

## Tasks

### Create Guided Flow

Implement:

```text
Connect Repo
→ Analyze
→ Generate Docs
→ Review
→ Enable Automation
```

---

### First-Time User Experience

Build:

* welcome screen
* onboarding states
* empty states
* progress indicators

---

### Improve Repo Creation UX

When repo added:

* fetch metadata automatically
* detect language/framework
* show repo summary
* suggest next action

---

### Contextual Navigation

Instead of generic tools:

* Search inside repo
* Analytics for repo
* Docs for repo

Everything should feel repo-centric.

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 2:

* users know what to do immediately
* product feels more guided
* less cognitive overload

---

# Sprint 3 — AI Experience Layer

## Duration: 7–10 days

## Goal

Make the AI feel intelligent and alive.

---

## Tasks

### AI Progress System

Replace generic loaders with staged progress:

```text
Scanning repository...
Analyzing architecture...
Generating README...
Creating API docs...
Opening PR...
```

---

### Add Activity Timeline

Show:

* recent generations
* sync history
* commits analyzed
* docs updated

---

### Add Background Status Indicators

Examples:

* monitoring repo
* indexing code
* webhook active
* sync healthy

---

### Add Toast/Feedback System

Success:

* Docs generated
* PR opened
* Sync complete

Failure:

* GitHub rate limit
* webhook failed
* parse issue

---

### Skeleton Loading States

For:

* analytics
* repo loading
* search results
* AI generation

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 3:

* AI feels alive
* app feels premium
* workflows feel smoother

---

# Sprint 4 — Autonomous Automation

## Duration: 7–14 days

## Goal

Transform AutoScribe from tool → autonomous system.

---

## Tasks

### Automatic Repo Monitoring

Detect:

* pushes
* PRs
* branch updates

---

### Background Documentation Sync

When code changes:

* detect affected files
* regenerate docs
* create/update PR automatically

---

### Smart Change Detection

Avoid regenerating everything.

Only update:

* changed modules
* affected README sections
* impacted APIs

---

### Automation Dashboard

Create dedicated area:

```text
Automation Status
- Monitoring active
- Last sync: 2m ago
- PRs opened: 4
- Docs freshness: 92%
```

---

### Automation Controls

User can:

* pause sync
* set branch rules
* enable auto-PR
* configure doc strategy

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 4:

* product becomes differentiated
* feels like infrastructure
* stronger startup positioning

---

# Sprint 5 — Product Polish

## Duration: 5–7 days

## Goal

Make the product emotionally polished.

---

## Tasks

### Motion & Transitions

Add subtle:

* page transitions
* hover states
* progress animations
* modal animations

---

### Premium UX Details

Add:

* command palette
* keyboard shortcuts
* repo quick switcher
* recent activity feed

---

### Better Analytics Storytelling

Instead of raw charts:
show insights.

Examples:

* README coverage increased 14%
* stale docs detected
* undocumented modules found

---

### Branding Consistency

Refine:

* iconography
* typography
* gradients
* spacing
* empty illustrations

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 5:

* app feels startup-grade
* emotionally polished
* memorable UX

---

# Sprint 6 — Launch Readiness

## Duration: 5–10 days

## Goal

Prepare for real users.

---

## Tasks

### Landing Page

Build:

* clear positioning
* feature explanation
* screenshots
* workflow demo

---

### Error Handling

Handle:

* failed GitHub auth
* invalid repo
* generation failures
* webhook issues

---

### Performance

Optimize:

* rerenders
* API calls
* loading speed
* caching

---

### User Trust

Add:

* logs
* audit history
* sync transparency
* AI explanation visibility

---

### Basic Usage Analytics

Track:

* repos connected
* docs generated
* user retention
* most used features

---

## Deliverable

At the end of Sprint 6:

* ready for beta users
* ready for portfolio/demo
* ready for indie launch

---

# Recommended Priority Order

| Priority               | Sprint   |
| ---------------------- | -------- |
| Critical               | Sprint 1 |
| Critical               | Sprint 2 |
| Very Important         | Sprint 3 |
| Biggest Differentiator | Sprint 4 |
| Polish                 | Sprint 5 |
| Launch                 | Sprint 6 |

---

# What NOT To Do Right Now

Avoid:

* adding random AI features
* building too many charts
* excessive customization
* enterprise settings
* multi-tenant complexity
* overengineering auth/billing

---

# The Main Product Strategy

## Your advantage is NOT:

```text
“we generate docs”
```

Many tools do that.

---

## Your advantage should become:

```text
“documentation stays updated automatically”
```

That’s the real startup opportunity.

---

# Final Product Direction

You should evolve AutoScribe into:

```text
AI-powered documentation infrastructure for GitHub repositories
```

NOT:

```text
documentation generator app
```

That positioning is much stronger.
